Fidelity choices worth knowing about:[0m[0m
- Bugs preserved: the inverted stored-block bounds test ([38;5;10mbits_left/8 <= LEN[0m), the [38;5;10mw = width + 1[0m off-by-one and the [38;5;10mpix_bytes[0m over-report passed to [38;5;10mcp_inflate[0m, the [38;5;10mtree[lo-1][0m read when a tree is empty, and the exact order of every validation check with its error string.[0m[0m
- Pointer arithmetic, integer truncation, and wrapping are mirrored ([38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m, [38;5;10mwrapping_offset[0m, [38;5;10mwrapping_shl[0m), and the in-place aliasing of [38;5;10mcp_convert[0m/[38;5;10mcp_depalette[0m/[38;5;10mcp_unfilter[0m over the [38;5;10mimg.pix[0m allocation is kept, so intermediate garbage in the row-slack column matches too. [38;5;10mmalloc[0m/[38;5;10mcalloc[0m/[38;5;10mfree[0m are the libc ones, so callers can [38;5;10mfree(img.pix)[0m.[0m[0m
- The C's [38;5;10massert()[0ms are treated as compiled out (NDEBUG release build) and left as comments. Where a corrupt stream would make C scribble past a stack array, I widened the local arrays instead so Rust cannot panic; that region is UB in C and not reproducible either way.[0m[0m
